{
 "source": "velvet_common.png",
 "notes": [
  "The rarity velvets the owner painted (Design Pack 2: common_grey ... special_red), one per tier, behind every item as the inventory painting paints its tiles: an item sits on its rarity's cloth.",
  "All seven cloths share one drape, so one region serves every tier: [230,40,800,800], the calm upper middle with the left fold and the swag's rim at the lower right -- it reads as velvet at 46 units and does not crowd the item at 240. Cut at 256, the largest window (the inventory list tile, 240), and only ever drawn down.",
  "tone brings each cloth to the tone of the painting's own tile for its tier (art/reference/inventory.png's seven tiles, measured away from the item): a gain per tier, then one vignette (strength 0.66 from 25% out) so the corners fall to about a third, as the painted tiles' do, and the item stands lit. Painted tile, max channel at its edge / by the item, against the cloth's centre: common 32/~45 vs 33 -> x1.45; uncommon 29/60 vs 47 -> x1.2; rare 40/56 vs 92 -> x0.9; epic 51/73 vs 71 -> x1.1; legendary 36/66 vs 200 -> x0.45 (a deep amber, so gold armour stays proud of it); mystic 84/128 vs 112 -> x0.8; special 41/59 vs 71 -> x1.0. The cloth keeps its own hue and weave: only its level moves.",
  "glow_<tier> is the same ground under a feathered ellipse, for a window with no ring of its own (the shop card's picture, the collection's painted frames): it fades into the window rather than ending in a square."
 ],
